{"ts":"2026-08-13T21:12:53.995Z","author":"codex","author_source":"configured","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"2a00cb64a3a7c61d1591525b","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-beads-yk8k"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Declaring the pm CLI as a runtime dependency gives consumers a second nested copy whenever their host pin differs"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"This package declared @unbrained/pm-cli in both dependencies and peerDependencies. The two ranges were separately satisfiable, so npm resolved them independently: a consumer installing the CLI at 2026.8.3, which satisfies this package's own declared peer floor, received the host copy at 2026.8.3 plus a nested 2026.8.13 under node_modules of this package. npm dedupes only when the ranges happen to overlap, so the tree is clean for some host pins and skewed for others. Skew matters here because consecutive CLI releases disagree about whether identical history bytes are fatal, a warning, or invisible, so which copy loads can decide a workspace gate verdict. The package is a pure extension with no bin entry, and sixteen sibling packages import the same SDK at runtime while declaring it only as a peer plus dev dependency."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["correctness","packaging"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-13T21:12:53.995Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-13T21:12:53.995Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"codex"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"ec522e69acffd3fe4d014f90fbfe3375f6315d